      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the expression \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula. The difference of squares formula states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\).\n\nFirst, apply the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = (235 - 221)(235 + 221)\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(235 - 221\\):\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(235 + 221\\):\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\nNow substitute these values back into the expression:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 14 \\times 456\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(14 \\times 456\\):\n\\[\n14 \\times 456 = 6384\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\) simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14}\n\\]\n\nNow, perform the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\) is \\(\\boxed{456}\\).\n\nTo confirm, let's check the calculation using Python:\n```python\n# Define the values\na = 235\nb = 221\n\n# Calculate the difference of squares\ndifference_of_squares = (a - b) * (a + b)\n\n# Divide by 14\nresult = difference_of_squares / 14\nprint(result)\n```",
